  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 143 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nHighly amplified upper ridge nosing into the western Plains will\nshift east and into our area tonight and tomorrow. Surface high\npressure extending from Ontario down into the upper midwest will\npush eastward slightly, allowing southerly winds to pick up. The\nupper ridge will flatten and move towards the Great Lakes on\nSunday, with southwesterly flow and then a weaker ridge into\nearly next week. The ridge starts to break down and upper low\npull out into the Plains late Wednesday, with still some\ndifferences in the exact track of the system. Confidence dips\neven lower on Friday with split flow and many of the ensemble\nmembers keeping the next upper low to our west, while two\nclusters have around 40 percent of the runs bringing troughing\nout into the Plains.\n\n...Warming trend into next week...\n\nAnother cold night tonight, although a bit less than last night\ndue to some high clouds and a bit more boundary layer mixing. \nHeights will rise through the weekend as ridging builds in \nbehind the departing Great Lakes low, and temps are expected to \nsee a warming trend with winds picking up from the south. ECMWF\nEFI have a good signal for warmth with 60 to 70 percent over\nclimo by the time Monday and Tuesday roll around. Much will\ndepend on cloud cover and precip chances, but even as the next\nsystem arrives mid to late week it seems eastern ND and western\nMN will remain in the warm sector. \n\n...Rain chances Wednesday night and Thursday...\n\nStill some variation in the exact track of the surface low for\nmid-week, and at least some of the model solutions keep our\nsouthern counties in the dry slot and don't give us much.\nProbabilities of at least measurable rain are 40 to 50 percent,\nbut over a tenth of an inch is below 20 percent. Still, this is\nthe most likely period in the next week of seeing moisture, and\nis worth a mention. Precipitation type given the unseasonably\nwarm temperatures looks to remain rain. A few of the ensemble\nmembers give a signal for some low probabilities of snow with \ncolder temps beyond day 7, but given low confidence in the \ncolder solutions out that far will hold off on mentioning \nanything impactful at this point.",
